    },
    "body": "Several entry points still instructed a continuing agent to repeat completed writer/dependent-read work and described an old cycle envelope as current. Align the README, roadmap, canonical plan, continuation prompt, contributor/workflow instructions and model/API lifecycle documentation with the source audit delivered in #1161.\n\nThe direction is a learned native geometric language model: shared typed selection, contextual transitions and emission, useful language/composition, measured laptop scaling, a qualified capability API, and then the same artifact in the GitHub Pages Studio. Geometric address/page selection is allowed; final serving excludes matrix products including lookup/add contractions and transformer backbones. Expert gates remain a conditional later option. Offline Rust training may use matmul.\n\nThe immediate implementation remains the observed numeric-versus-word selection boundary, preserving distinct NoOperation/NoRead semantics, correct cases and exact causal provenance. Current-state remains the artifact pointer. Historical results, the roadmap archive and dated GitHub/JSON snapshots remain preserved; historical budget figures are explicitly not fresh execution admission.\n\nValidation: existing Rust architecture-policy checker and claim-wording check pass; 19 added relative links and heading fragments, all 98 source-manifest hashes, historical roadmap byte preservation and diff whitespace checks pass. No Rust source changes, local model builds, training or inference. Cumulative model ledger unchanged at 3,605.626/4,170 seconds. No capability issue is closed.\n\nRefs #820, #973, #1139, #1140.\n",
